    <h1>Brain Puzzle 3 Level 138 Answer: Beach Lifeguard</h1>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with the developer of Brain Puzzle 3.</div>

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>Twelve moves and the beach goes quiet. Ring first, then the lifeguard's red vest, both to the swimmer yelling in the water. Bucket into the sea, then the full bucket onto the grill. Whistle to the lifeguard. Meat to the swimmer the fin circles. Cloud over the sunburned kid at the bottom left. Tap the first-aid kit, then bandage the bruised man face-down at the water's edge. Ointment and the cold drink to the tourist at the top of the water, and the phone to the lifeguard.</p>
    </div>
    <style is:global>
.answer-inline{margin:.55rem 0 0;padding:.6rem .9rem;background: #FFFBF2; border: 1px solid #F0DFAE; border-radius: 10px}
.answer-inline p{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:#7A6A5C}
.answer-inline a{color:#B45309;font-weight:800;text-decoration:underline}
    </style>
    <div class="answer-inline">
      <p>Got it? If you enjoy these, try <a href="/akari/">Akari</a>: our own free browser puzzle with a fresh grid every midnight. No app, no sign-up.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="verify-note">How this page was built: our reference clip (embedded below) is 1:55 of unedited play, cut into one frame per second and read by hand. The twelve moves are the level's own hint list; the timestamps on the cards mark the moments we could confirm on screen, and the player's own order wanders between them.</div>

    <h2>Watch the full solution<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>One beach, eight tourists in trouble and one lifeguard on a chair. The clip is the fastest way to see which hand goes where.</p>
