    <h2>Level 138 walkthrough, move by move<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <!-- frame refs: hero=f_0001 (t=0s), step1=f_0027 (t=26s), shark=f_0038 (t=37s), grill=f_0083 (t=82s), phone=f_0096 (t=95s), cloud=f_0110 (t=109s), result=f_0115 (t=114s) -->
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 &middot; 0:21</span>
      <strong>Drag the swim ring off the chair to the swimmer with both arms up</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l138_step1_ring.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 138 step 1 — swim ring on the swimmer" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" />
      <p>The red and white ring starts the level hanging on the lifeguard chair. It belongs to the swimmer in the middle of the water, and once he has it the caption under him reads "I'm saved!". In our frames he keeps it around him for the rest of the level, so if your ring is still on the chair, you have not handed it over yet.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uER0OztTH8&t=21s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:21</a></p>
    </div>
    <InContentAd />
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2</span>
      <strong>Then the lifeguard's red life vest, to the same swimmer</strong>
      <p>The ring is not the only thing that goes into the water. The vest the lifeguard is wearing comes off him and goes to that same swimmer, which is why the chair looks bare by the end of a clean run. It is a drag, not a tap: press the vest, not the man.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3</span>
      <strong>Bucket into the sea, then the full bucket onto the grill</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l138_step_grill.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 138 step 3 — the grill and the red bucket" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" />
      <p>Two moves, one object. Drag the red bucket from the sand into the water, and it comes back full; drag that full bucket onto the grill and the flames die. An empty bucket over the grill does nothing, which is the single most common dead end in this level. The Hawaiian-shirt cook spent the whole level with his hands on his head for a reason.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 &middot; 0:35</span>
      <strong>Whistle to the lifeguard, and the fin leaves the water</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l138_shark_gone.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 138 step 4 — the shark fin is gone" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" />
      <p>Drag the whistle that hangs around the lifeguard's neck to the lifeguard himself and he uses it. In our clip the grey fin that started the level behind the left swimmer is already gone from the water at 0:35, with "The shark is gone" under the scene.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uER0OztTH8&t=35s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:35</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5</span>
      <strong>Meat from the grill to the swimmer the fin is circling</strong>
      <p>The steak on the grill is not decoration. It goes to the swimmer who has a fin behind him, and that is the move that ends the "shark" problem for good. If the grill is still loaded and the swimmer still has a fin, this is the pair you have not matched yet.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 &middot; 1:33</span>
      <strong>Park the cloud over the sunburned kid at the bottom left</strong>
