      <p>There is one loose cloud in the sky and one kid on the sand, red from head to toe with heat lines coming off him. Drag the cloud down and it settles over him like a shade; the caption changes to "I feel much cooler". It is the only object in the sky that answers a drag.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uER0OztTH8&t=93s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">1:33</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 &middot; 0:25</span>
      <strong>Tap the first-aid kit, then bandage the bruised man</strong>
      <p>The white kit with the red cross sits at the foot of the lifeguard chair and it is a tap, not a drag: open it and it offers its contents. In our frames it is already standing open by 0:25. The man who needs the bandage is the one lying face-down at the water's edge with the purple bruise; after he is patched the caption goes to "Call an ambulance!" at 1:13.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uER0OztTH8&t=25s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">0:25</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8</span>
      <strong>Ointment and the cold drink, both to the tourist at the top of the water</strong>
      <p>Two objects, one target: the tube from the kit and the glass with the orange drink that stands on the grill shelf. Both go to the tourist at the top of the water, the one who is not waving but holding himself. Ointment first, drink second; swapping them does not register.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 9 &middot; 1:35</span>
      <strong>Phone to the lifeguard</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l138_step_phone.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 138 step 9 — the lifeguard on the phone" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" />
      <p>The phone starts on the sand next to the sunburned kid. Hand it to the lifeguard and he puts it to his ear, "Someone needs help". This is the move that pulls the level towards its ending: the polaroid follows a few seconds later.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uER0OztTH8&t=95s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">1:35</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 &middot; 1:53</span>
      <strong>Level complete</strong>
      <img src="/brain-puzzle-3/l138_result.jpg" alt="Brain Puzzle 3 level 138 result screen" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" />
      <p>The shot freezes into the polaroid, confetti drops and "Another productive day." lands under the scene. Tap Next for level 139.</p>
      <p class="ts">Video check: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uER0OztTH8&t=113s" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">1:53</a></p>
    </div>

    <h2>What makes Beach Lifeguard tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>This is the busiest opening scene in the game so far: eight people in trouble at once and no arrow pointing at any of them. The camera gives you a grill, a swimmer with a fin, a sunburned kid, a man with a bruise, a lifeguard, a whistle, a ring, a bucket, a cloud and a phone, and the level never says which problem it wants first. It wants all of them, one object per person, and the scene only goes quiet when the last one is matched.</p>
    <p>The trap is the bucket. Every other object in the level is a single drag from where it stands to the person who needs it, but the bucket has to make two trips: out into the sea to fill, then back onto the grill. Anyone who drags an empty bucket straight at the flames gets nothing, no error message, no animation, and reads it as the wrong object rather than the wrong order. It is the same lesson the game teaches in the level where you have to fill something before you can use it.</p>
    <p>The second trap is that the first-aid kit is a tap. Nine of the twelve moves are drags and the eye stops reading the kit as interactive at all, because it never moves. Open it, then drag the bandage out of it. And the two most similar-looking passengers, the swimmer yelling in the middle and the one at the top holding himself, want different things: ring and vest for the first, ointment and drink for the second.</p>

    <h2>Twelve moves in this order<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The order below is the level's own hint list. Our clip wanders between those beats because the player idles between moves, so treat the timestamps as reference points rather than a schedule.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Swim ring to the swimmer in the middle.</li>
      <li>Lifeguard's red vest to the same swimmer.</li>
      <li>Bucket into the sea, then the full bucket onto the grill.</li>
      <li>Whistle to the lifeguard.</li>
      <li>Meat to the swimmer with the fin behind him.</li>
      <li>Cloud over the sunburned kid.</li>
      <li>Tap the first-aid kit.</li>
      <li>Bandage to the bruised man at the water's edge.</li>
      <li>Ointment to the tourist at the top of the water.</li>
      <li>Cold drink to the same tourist.</li>
      <li>Phone to the lifeguard.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No hints, no hidden objects: everything you need is visible in the first frame of the clip.</p>

